course: dictionary
lesson: 15802
title: Knowing and not knowing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unaware is made of un- and aware. Un- means not, and aware means knowing about something. So unaware means not knowing about something, or not noticing it. «Sam was unaware of the puddle, so he walked straight into it.» Sam did not know the puddle was there.
explain: Look at the words that come after unaware. It is often followed by of or that: «unaware of» and «unaware that». «She was unaware that the door was open.» Try swapping in not knowing: she was not knowing that the door was open. The meaning still fits.
explain: Unawares is a different form, an adverb, and it has a special phrase: «take someone unawares» or «caught unawares». It means by surprise, without warning. «The sudden rain caught us unawares.» Nobody warned us; it simply happened.
fact: Unaware means not knowing about something, or not noticing it.
fact: Un- at the start of a word often means not, as in unhappy and unsafe.
fact: «Unaware» is often followed by «of» or «that», as in «unaware of the danger».
fact: «Unawares» is an adverb meaning by surprise, as in «caught unawares».
fact: Writers use unaware to build suspense: the reader knows the danger, but the character is unaware of it.
exercise: «The cat was unaware of the mouse hiding under the table.» What does unaware mean here? | Chasing the mouse happily | Hungry for dinner | *Not knowing about the mouse | Asleep on the sofa
exercise: «The storm caught the campers unawares.» What does caught unawares mean? | Slowly and carefully | *By surprise, without warning | Warned in advance | Lost in the woods
exercise: «She was unaware ___ the gate was open.» Which word fits best in the gap? | with | at | from | *that
test: «Ben was unaware of the wet floor, and he slipped.» What does unaware mean? | *Not noticing the wet floor | Very tired | Cleaning the wet floor | Watching the wet floor closely
test: Which phrase means without warning? | take someone's time | *take someone unawares | take someone's side | take someone home
exam: «The thief came in unawares while the family slept.» What does unawares mean? | Quietly, without a sound | Slowly, one at a time | Angrily | *By surprise, without warning
